DONE: Investigated why searches don't appear in frontend — traced flow from frontend API call to backend providers. Found all providers return 0 jobs; Greenhouse (only provider with real data, 969 jobs from Stripe) timed out at 10s. Fixed: parallelized company requests with Promise.allSettled in Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workday. Increased Greenhouse timeout to 30s. Fixed param naming mismatch (excludeCompanies→excludedCompanies, trustMin→minTrustScore) with backward-compatible aliases. Fixed frontend tsconfig for build errors. All 187 tests pass. Live test confirms 2,445 jobs returned.
WRONG: Original sequential iteration was a performance anti-pattern across all providers. Timeouts were set aggressively without testing real API response times. Parameter names inconsistent between frontend/backend. Lost time wrestling PowerShell background processes for testing instead of using a direct approach.
IMPROV: Add integration tests with realistic provider API timings. Start with a real HTTP request when debugging search issues. Standardize param naming across layers from the start. Use Node.js for API testing instead of PowerShell.
LEARN: Greenhouse needs ~18-20s for 13 companies. Promise.allSettled is better than for...of for independent requests. Two timeout layers exist: axios-level (PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_MS) kills individual HTTP requests, executeIsolatedProvider timeout kills the entire provider. Trust scoring gives reasonable scores (7.5-8.4) for well-known companies like Stripe/Airbnb.
NEXT: Fix pagination — page 2 returns 0 jobs (possible cache key issue). Fix broken providers (Gupy 400, Workday 422, Ashby/Lever 404) that return 0 jobs. Run Playwright check for frontend integration. Monitor Greenhouse rate limits under parallel requests.
